load @term/form/code/vibe/dock
  find dock

# The knit, the law of motion, the sixth base element. Each beat it has two steps. Collide, the two tones meeting head on in each line rearrange by a fixed permutation. Then stream, each site hands its tone one dock onward to the matching site of its neighbor. The knit is the unique local reversible rule symmetric under the full symmetry of the cell, forced not chosen.
form knit
  link dock, like dock

# The knit, proof-checked by `seed test`: the law of motion, two steps each beat, collide then stream, 2 = 1 + 1. The
# claim that the knit is REVERSIBLE is proved in `code/vibe/tone`: the collide step on a line is an involution
# (`collide-is-reversible`, collide twice returns the original), built from the tone mirror being order two, so the law
# can run either way locally and the arrow comes only from the wake's one-way growth, not from the motion.
hold knit-has-two-steps-beat
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call add
      code 1
      code 1
